{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>You shall rise before the aged</b> — a warning to an elder not to be burdensome." "<b>You shall rise before the aged</b> — and adjacent to it: <i>When a stranger resides with you</i> — to say: even before an aged ignaramus." "<b>I am YHWH</b> — and adjacent to it: <i>When a stranger resides with you</i> — to say: whoever perverts the judgment of a stranger, it is as though he perverts the judgment of the Holy One, blessed be He."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:06.129393953Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}